# Enums & labels

No `@nuxtjs/i18n`. User-facing strings are **Arabic** inline or in label maps.

## Enums ([`app/enums/`](mdc:app/enums/))

Match backend string values. Prefer:

1. Const map (`Object.freeze` in `.js`, or `as const` in `.ts`)
2. Type alias from values (TS)
3. `*_LABELS` / options / `isX` + `normalizeX` helpers

```ts
// ✅ app/enums/operationActivity.ts style
export const OperationActivity = {
  SALE: "SALE",
  RESERVATION: "RESERVATION",
} as const;
export type OperationActivity =
  (typeof OperationActivity)[keyof typeof OperationActivity];
```

```js
// ✅ app/enums/userRole.js — also USER_ROLE_LABELS + USER_ROLE_LAYOUT
export const UserRole = Object.freeze({
  ADMIN: "ADMIN",
  CUSTOMER_SERVICE: "CUSTOMER_SERVICE",
  BRANCH_EMPLOYEE: "BRANCH_EMPLOYEE",
});
```

```ts
// ❌ TypeScript `enum` keyword, or English-only UI labels for domain status
```

## Domain labels & tags

- Status / metric Arabic copy: [`app/utils/domain-labels/`](mdc:app/utils/domain-labels/) + `getLabel` in [`shared.js`](mdc:app/utils/domain-labels/shared.js)
- Tag presentation: [`app/utils/status-tags/`](mdc:app/utils/status-tags/)
- Money/date/number display: [`app/utils/format/`](mdc:app/utils/format/)

When adding a backend status value, update the enum **and** the matching label/tag map.
